 "root_cause": {
  "finding": "D2's library clips (31_meshy_fetch.py) were fetched on rig 01a0eb6a -- nb_t8 work/res_rig.json, the MESHY-mesh candidate -- not the chosen Tripo body's rig 01a0eb7e (work/res_rig_tripo.json). Their skeleton's rest differs from the body's (hips-to-head 54.49 vs 56.55 units; upper arms 12-15 deg; hips rest rotation ~110 deg), and 33_assemble's Blender merge then copied actions in bone pose space across the mismatched rests: every merged clip equals Q_body = R_body_rest . R_src_rest^-1 . Q_src to 0.00 deg.",
  "instrument": "so_d7/scripts/s16_clip_fidelity.py (joints in the hips' LOCAL frame) is only valid when both rigs share the hips rest frame; across these rigs it reads 2.4-2.9 even on a faithful graft. nb_d2/scripts/56_clip_fidelity.py: the hips' PHYSICAL frame (x_j = R_hips_rest_world . G_hips^-1 . p_j). Across two rigs with different rest SHAPES any position measure has a floor (~0.24 here, measured on a faithful world-space graft) -- so the fix was to fetch on the body's own rig, where the measure reads 0.0001.",
  "credits": "18 of the 21: 15 for five re-fetches on the body rig (walk_fight 21, block1 138, shield_push 220, double_combo 92, axe_stance 85) + 3 WASTED by an accidental fetch (action 1 on the old rig, anims/nothing.glb): a command meant to test 31's new wrong-rig refusal ran before the refusal was in the file"
 },
